# Frontend Conventions: packages/web

## Component Structure
- Function components only, no class components, per this project's
  existing pattern.
- One component per file, file name matches the component name
  (`RouteCard.tsx` exports `RouteCard`).
- Presentational components (e.g. `RouteCard`) receive data as props
  and do not fetch data themselves. Only container/page-level components
  (e.g. `RouteDashboard`) own data fetching.

## Accessibility
- Every interactive element (button, link, input) must have an
  accessible name, either visible text or an `aria-label`.
- Every image needs an `alt` attribute; decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Loading and error states must be announced to assistive tech, e.g. a
  `role="status"` on a loading indicator, not just a visual spinner.

## API Usage
- Components never call `fetch` directly. All backend calls go through
  a typed function in `src/api/` (e.g. `routesApi.ts`), matching the
  existing pattern.
- The shape of any data returned from `src/api/` must match the backend
  contract in `packages/api/src/types/route.types.ts` exactly. If a
  field doesn't exist on the backend type, don't invent it on the
  frontend.

## State Management
- Prefer a dedicated data-fetching hook (see `src/hooks/`) over ad-hoc
  `useState` + `useEffect` fetch logic duplicated in a component.
